1
00:00:00,974 --> 00:00:02,444
(Raj:)Maybe you don't want

2
00:00:02,442 --> 00:00:03,612
(Raj:)someone exactly like you.

3
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:05,510
You know what they say:
opposites attract.

4
00:00:05,511 --> 00:00:07,441
(Sheldon:)Well, by that logic,

5
00:00:07,447 --> 00:00:10,917
(Sheldon:)I should be with someone short,
dull and needy, eh?

6
00:00:10,917 --> 00:00:12,317
(Sheldon:)Not to cast aspersions,

7
00:00:12,318 --> 00:00:16,618
(Sheldon:)but I can't shake a stick around
here without hitting that.

8
00:00:20,459 --> 00:00:23,099
(Dave:)You know, I once
drove 500 miles

9
00:00:23,096 --> 00:00:26,066
(Dave:)to hear him speak
at Stanford.

10
00:00:26,065 --> 00:00:29,065
(Amy:)I have a DVD of that lecture.

11
00:00:29,068 --> 00:00:31,068
(Dave:)Really? Wasn't it great?

12
00:00:31,070 --> 00:00:34,710
(Amy:)Not as a Valentine's
present, no.

13
00:00:34,707 --> 00:00:36,437
(Dave:)Well, the next time
you watch it,

14
00:00:36,442 --> 00:00:38,212
(Dave:)I'm the bloke who
asked the question

15
00:00:38,211 --> 00:00:41,211
(Dave:)that he said was
stupid and obvious.

16
00:00:41,214 --> 00:00:44,514
(Dave:)It was the nicest thing
he said to anyone there.

17
00:00:44,517 --> 00:00:46,347
(Amy:)That's, um, terrific.

18
00:00:46,352 --> 00:00:49,222
Listen, I'm-I'm kind of tired.
Can we call it a night?

19
00:00:49,222 --> 00:00:51,622
(Dave:)Oh, gosh. Sorry,
I've just spent the whole night

20
00:00:51,624 --> 00:00:53,594
(Dave:)talking about your ex-boyfriend.

21
00:00:53,593 --> 00:00:54,993
(Dave:)I'm such an idiot.

22
00:00:54,994 --> 00:00:56,924
(Amy:)No, you're not.

23
00:00:56,930 --> 00:00:59,860
(Dave:)Well, maybe not an idiot,
but certainly not as smart as...

24
00:00:59,866 --> 00:01:01,636
(Dave:)someone we won't mention.

